<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Allada</h1><p class="st-meta">1440 CE – 1724 CE (approx.) · capital Allada</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Aja kingdom of the Slave Coast, the leading slave-trading state of the area in the 17th century and the ancestral seat of Dahomey's kings.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allada">Allada</a> was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aja-people">Aja</a> migrants from Tado, west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mono-river">Mono river</a>, traditionally in the 15th century. Tradition links its royal line, descended from the founding ancestor Agassu, to the later rulers of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-dahomey">Kingdom of Dahomey</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-porto-novo">Kingdom of Porto-Novo</a>, which branched off from Allada in the 17th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allada">Allada's</a> king, known to Europeans as the king of Ardra, controlled the coast through the port of Offra and dealt with Portuguese, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, English and French traders, becoming a major source of enslaved people by the 1640s. In 1670 Allada sent an ambassador to the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>. Vodun cults and royal ancestor worship underpinned kingship.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1724 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agaja">Agaja</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allada">Allada</a>, which was absorbed into his kingdom. The town remains a ritual centre, and the Allada dynasty is recognised as the ancestor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin's</a> royal houses.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1440 CE – 1724 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:88.36%;width:5.65%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1440 CE – 1724 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Allada</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Vodun</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gbe (Aja)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/benin">Benin</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Allada, Ardra, Arda</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1582&amp;focus=kingdom-of-allada" aria-label="Kingdom of Allada on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4740 1928 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Allada lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5060 2184L5109 2141M5060 2184L5055 2165M5060 2184L5058 2194"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5109 2141h0M5055 2165h0M5058 2194h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5060 2184h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5060 2184h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Allada. <a href="/atlas?year=1582&amp;focus=kingdom-of-allada">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

